# Working fast

- A small task (a config entry and a test) should take under 30 minutes.
  If you pass 45 minutes, or the same step fails twice, stop and write down
  what's blocking you. Don't keep trying.
- Plan first, in three lines: the files you'll change, the test you'll add,
  the one command that proves it works. Then do exactly that.
- Never read `src/Game.js` (7,800 lines), `src/ui/UIManager.js` or
  `src/duilt/DuiltGame.js` whole. Search them and read only the lines
  around what you found.
- Read each file you need once. Don't re-read a file you just edited to
  check it.
- Don't refactor, rename, reformat or tidy anything the task doesn't name.
- When the task's "Done when" list is met, stop: commit, push, open the
  pull request. Don't polish.

# Tests

- While working, run only the test file you changed:
  `node tests/<name>.test.mjs`. It takes under a second.
- Run the full suite, `node tests/run.mjs` (about 5 minutes), once, at the
  end. If something fails, fix it, re-run just that test file, then the full
  suite once more. Never run the full suite more than twice in a task.
- A failing test in code you didn't touch: say so in the pull request.
  Don't try to fix it.
- Don't start the dev server or open a browser unless the task says it's
  needed.

# Git

- Start each task from fresh main:
  `git checkout main && git pull origin main && git checkout -b cline/<short-task-name>`.
  Then check `git branch --show-current` is not main.
- If the working tree has changes before you start, stop and ask me.
- Never commit or push to main. Never force-push, rewrite history or merge.
- Check `git diff --staged` before each commit. Never commit `.env`, keys
  or tokens.
- One commit per task is fine. The message says why, in plain English.
- At the end: `git push -u origin <branch>`, then open a pull request with
  `gh pr create --fill` if `gh` is installed. If it isn't, give me this
  link to open one:
  `https://github.com/bernardogomesnunes/GameNew/compare/<branch>?expand=1`.
- On a merge conflict, or a git error you don't understand, stop and ask
  me.

# The rest

Read `docs/cline-tasks.md` for the tasks, the game's rules and the code
style.
